; 07-show.kurt

; Every claim so far (`A`, `B`, `A and B`, ...) was checked immediately
; against the current theory.  `show` instead states a *goal* explicitly; you
; then justify it step by step inside a `proof` block (08-proof.kurt), which
; usually ends with `qed` (09-qed.kurt; `qed` is optional).  This lesson
; already uses `proof` and `qed`; the next two lessons explain them.

bool A, B

use A implies B
use A

show B
proof
    B
qed

; `show` also accepts a label, just like `use`:
bool C
use B implies C
show C  "chained-modus-ponens"
proof
    C
qed
